From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "sh.chao" <sh.chao@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 22:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Veloce r25-3-0114: share exact immutable Form programs

Promote fully native, resource-independent Form RenderPrograms from holder-
local ownership to a bounded document cache. Repeated equivalent Form
invocations keep their canonical PDFium object holders but skip duplicate
native geometry copying, state interning, hashing, spatial-index construction,
and retained allocation.

Cache identity covers the source stream generation, Form matrix and bounding
box, transparency semantics, parent matrix, and every inherited path state
consumed by exact lowering. Resource lookups, inherited clips, partial native
coverage, stream mutation, command-count changes, and global object mutation
all fail closed to normal holder construction and canonical rendering.

Keep at most 16 entries and 96 MiB of cache-owned programs per document.
Programs contain no page-object pointers; live holders remain authoritative for
visibility, editing, canonical fallback, and source ordering. Add tests for
exact reuse and stream-mutation invalidation.
---
